1
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:06,400
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

2
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:09,210
(Get ready, dig your anger up, MOB!)

3
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:12,060
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

4
00:00:12,060 --> 00:00:13,120
(Get ready!)

5
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:18,710
Coming down, could you fill your satisfaction?

6
00:00:19,770 --> 00:00:24,450
You're a MOB. Can't you feel your own frustration?

7
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:30,200
Coming down, could you fill your satisfaction?

8
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:34,760
You're a MOB. What do you want to be?

9
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:41,300
Wear your overflowing emotions on your sleeve and break it down.

10
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:46,200
What do you see once you go beyond your limits?

11
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:49,180
(99.9! 99.9!)

12
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:52,060
The mysterious percentage.

13
00:00:53,740 --> 00:00:56,530
Cryin' my life, cryin' my psyche,

14
00:00:56,530 --> 00:00:59,480
cryin' my heart in such commonplaces!

15
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:02,310
Is that your ideal? Is that your mind?

16
00:01:02,310 --> 00:01:05,220
It all begins when it hits 100.

17
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:08,010
The MOB is alive. The MOB is high.

18
00:01:08,010 --> 00:01:10,900
The MOB is staying frustrated, aren't you?

19
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:15,290
Is that your ideal? Is that your mind? Right now...

20
00:01:16,610 --> 00:01:17,830
Your life is your own.

21
00:01:17,830 --> 00:01:20,600
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

22
00:01:20,270 --> 00:01:25,110
Mob Psycho

23
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:23,490
(Get ready, dig your anger up, MOB!)

24
00:01:23,490 --> 00:01:26,360
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

25
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:27,670
(Get ready!)

26
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:33,980
Boss Fight
~The Final Light~

27
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:39,800
Now I'll be able to hit
you with everything...

28
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:42,930
My powers... and my rage.

29
00:01:51,170 --> 00:01:52,630
Output 20%

30
00:01:57,470 --> 00:01:58,800
Is that it?

31
00:02:04,430 --> 00:02:06,820
This is finally getting interesting.

32
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:20,990
You're...

33
00:02:21,740 --> 00:02:24,170
You're enjoying this too, aren't you?

34
00:02:27,490 --> 00:02:29,500
What the hell is going on?

35
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:31,900
They're fighting in
a whole different stratosphere!

36
00:02:35,830 --> 00:02:40,550
As righteous as you try to sound,
deep down, you're the same as me.

37
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:45,570
Nii-san!

38
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:48,810
How does it feel to be released
from your shackles?

39
00:02:48,810 --> 00:02:51,520
We are freer than anyone else!

40
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:55,370
Nii-san...

41
00:03:12,870 --> 00:03:15,840
How... How could I...

42
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:17,830
How could I be so foolish?

43
00:03:18,850 --> 00:03:23,440
It may have only been for a moment,
but I let this power control me!

44
00:03:26,330 --> 00:03:28,310
You're so emotionally unstable.

45
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:33,750
At this rate, you'll never catch up to me,
no matter how far you go.

46
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:35,910
I am the best in the world!

47
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:41,860
How did your life end up being so hollow?

48
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:46,340
I can't judge you for the life
you chose, though.

49
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:48,840
You were just unlucky.

50
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:51,920
What are you talking about?

51
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:56,340
There is no one in this world
that is as lucky as me!

52
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:57,800
Output 50%

53
00:03:58,340 --> 00:04:00,510
Heaven bestowed these powers upon me

54
00:04:00,510 --> 00:04:06,200
and made you all extras,
created solely to make my star shine!

55
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:10,060
Really? Then it wasn't luck
that you were lacking.

56
00:04:10,730 --> 00:04:11,580
It was bonds.

57
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:13,730
What?

58
00:04:14,090 --> 00:04:17,690
You were the only one
who existed in your world.

59
00:04:18,190 --> 00:04:20,290
You lived in overwhelming solitude.

60
00:04:21,830 --> 00:04:23,180
I know that feeling well...

61
00:04:23,490 --> 00:04:26,470
Living in a world where I'm completely alone,
one I want to forget forever.

62
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:30,600
I don't understand.

63
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:31,610
Why?

64
00:04:31,610 --> 00:04:33,450
Why are you crying?

65
00:04:35,370 --> 00:04:38,210
You might not believe me,

66
00:04:38,570 --> 00:04:41,920
but I really don't want to hurt you.

67
00:05:04,550 --> 00:05:05,320
I'm sorry...

68
00:05:12,880 --> 00:05:15,090
What the hell is going on?

69
00:05:15,090 --> 00:05:16,710
Don't ask me.

70
00:05:17,010 --> 00:05:19,790
The president's aura is gone.

71
00:05:19,790 --> 00:05:22,270
Does that mean it's over?

72
00:05:22,940 --> 00:05:23,900
Yes!

73
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:27,530
Impressive. Is that boy actually human?

74
00:05:27,530 --> 00:05:29,930
He's just a normal middle school kid.

75
00:05:30,270 --> 00:05:34,320
Nii-san... You used a tremendous
amount of power again.

76
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:35,770
It's not over yet.

77
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:39,200
My dad's aura didn't disappear.

78
00:05:39,790 --> 00:05:41,020
It changed.

79
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:48,080
My dad mentioned before that
he picked up the habit of only awakening

80
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:49,920
when put under a lot of stress.

81
00:06:22,110 --> 00:06:24,230
This goes beyond human understanding.

82
00:06:24,230 --> 00:06:27,700
How can one man's powers be so immense?

83
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:32,160
Shigeo... This is the one day in your life
you shouldn't try to do the impossible.

84
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:36,450
He's already using way more power
than he did when beat me.

85
00:06:37,350 --> 00:06:38,950
If you can't win, run.

86
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:42,630
You're not responsible for any of this,

87
00:06:43,340 --> 00:06:44,080
Mob.

88
00:06:46,980 --> 00:06:48,970
I've never felt like this before.

89
00:06:50,850 --> 00:06:52,070
Wake up.

90
00:06:52,070 --> 00:06:55,310
Don't think I'm going to let you say
you're done already.

91
00:06:57,090 --> 00:06:59,040
Wake up!

92
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:00,090
No.

93
00:07:01,010 --> 00:07:02,060
As much as I hate to admit it,

94
00:07:02,550 --> 00:07:04,450
I'm not strong enough.

95
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:09,280
I don't have the power to show you a new path.

96
00:07:11,010 --> 00:07:15,710
You awakened my destructive impulses,
now you have to deal with them!

97
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:19,170
Don't go hiding in your shell now!

98
00:07:26,370 --> 00:07:27,680
I give up.

99
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:32,670
I hoped that you could turn over a new leaf
and become a better person,

100
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:34,460
but that hope's gone now!

101
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:42,660
I-It appears... that we're both...

102
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:47,230
influencing each other quite a bit...

103
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:51,560
Yes. But I couldn't be a good influence.

104
00:07:51,970 --> 00:07:54,450
I'm done. We can both lose at this point.

105
00:07:58,160 --> 00:07:59,620
Output 100%

106
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:00,630
This is...

107
00:08:05,790 --> 00:08:07,710
I might actually die...

108
00:08:08,310 --> 00:08:09,050
Mob!

109
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:13,010
Shigeo.

110
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:14,110
Nii-san!

111
00:08:14,110 --> 00:08:14,840
Heya.

112
00:08:15,010 --> 00:08:16,300
Well done.

113
00:08:17,250 --> 00:08:18,640
No, this is nothing.

114
00:08:19,530 --> 00:08:21,500
Nothing compared to the fear
of losing all I have.

115
00:08:38,820 --> 00:08:42,710
Body improvement! Fight on!

116
00:09:12,090 --> 00:09:13,200
I'll defeat you!

117
00:09:22,660 --> 00:09:24,830
If something like that makes it outside...

118
00:09:27,410 --> 00:09:28,830
It'll explode...

119
00:09:32,350 --> 00:09:33,760
It'll explode?

120
00:09:34,090 --> 00:09:36,310
Oh, it'll explode!

121
00:09:37,620 --> 00:09:41,070
Run away! Everyone, run away!

122
00:09:41,070 --> 00:09:41,960
Mob!

123
00:09:41,960 --> 00:09:43,140
You're alive!

124
00:09:43,670 --> 00:09:46,800
He ended up releasing too much
energy and self-destructed!

125
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:48,420
You're bleeding like crazy!

126
00:09:48,420 --> 00:09:50,650
Master, please run!

127
00:09:51,190 --> 00:09:53,480
All that's left is an
excessive amount of energy.

128
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,540
I'm pretty sure an explosion will happen,

129
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:58,110
a huge one at that!

130
00:09:59,750 --> 00:10:02,040
So you're saying we won't
be able to contain it.

131
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:03,120
Let's hurry!

132
00:10:05,650 --> 00:10:06,480
Ritsu.

133
00:10:06,820 --> 00:10:09,600
Let's run. We're gonna get caught
up in that if we stay here.

134
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:13,740
That's the president's final light...

135
00:10:13,740 --> 00:10:16,310
Our president who was trying
to take over the world...

136
00:10:16,310 --> 00:10:18,840
Just shut up and run! You're gonna die!

137
00:10:19,030 --> 00:10:21,500
Huh? Hey, where's Shigeo?

138
00:10:24,060 --> 00:10:26,340
You made the right choice.

139
00:10:26,340 --> 00:10:27,960
There's no way to avoid this.

140
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:31,360
Your only choice is to end my life—
to sever the energy source—

141
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:33,800
before the explosion happens.

142
00:10:35,870 --> 00:10:37,110
What are you doing?

143
00:10:37,110 --> 00:10:38,650
I'm going to contain the explosion.

144
00:10:39,970 --> 00:10:42,820
In the end, you aren't able to defeat me,

145
00:10:42,820 --> 00:10:47,790
save your friends, or save yourself.

146
00:10:47,790 --> 00:10:51,750
With your powers, you should've
been able to handle this better.

147
00:10:51,750 --> 00:10:55,000
Just having powers doesn't mean
everything works out for you.

148
00:10:55,300 --> 00:10:57,640
But that's perfectly fine,

149
00:10:58,870 --> 00:11:02,480
as long as you make
the important choices yourself.

150
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:06,430
I'm the protagonist of my own life.

151
00:11:08,270 --> 00:11:10,440
That's why I chose to be here.

152
00:11:10,950 --> 00:11:15,390
No matter how much I dislike you,
to leave you to suffer on your own

153
00:11:15,390 --> 00:11:17,060
would just be too sad.

154
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:20,130
So I'm going to help you.

155
00:11:23,250 --> 00:11:26,050
What do you plan to do with that filthy cat?

156
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:30,520
Well, the poor thing was drenched
and shivering in the rain.

157
00:11:30,980 --> 00:11:32,120
And think about it...

158
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:35,340
Sho will grow up into a gentle boy.

159
00:11:35,650 --> 00:11:38,300
He's going to grow up watching you, after all.

160
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:40,980
We need to be gentle. Gentle.

161
00:11:41,800 --> 00:11:44,180
Why did you have to be so violent?!

162
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:50,020
To lead an organization,
I need to establish my dominance.

163
00:11:50,020 --> 00:11:52,730
You can't move people's hearts
with psychic powers!

164
00:11:52,730 --> 00:11:55,360
No, power is absolute.

165
00:11:55,570 --> 00:11:59,320
As long as I have this power,
people will follow me.

166
00:11:59,590 --> 00:12:02,100
You think that's true for everyone?

167
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:03,030
I do.

168
00:12:03,310 --> 00:12:06,450
Sho is also showing interest
in my powers as well.

169
00:12:06,450 --> 00:12:07,530
Goodbye.

170
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:15,220
When did I...

171
00:12:20,170 --> 00:12:21,940
If I can absorb it...

172
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:24,470
Don't. You'll just end up...

173
00:12:27,820 --> 00:12:29,780
You wanted to apologize, didn't you?!

174
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:34,240
Then you need to say it loud and clear!

175
00:12:37,870 --> 00:12:41,010
That's right. I also...

176
00:12:41,780 --> 00:12:45,940
I also have someone I need
to express my feelings to!

177
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:09,660
Mob...

178
00:13:11,430 --> 00:13:14,940
Mob Psycho

179
00:13:14,940 --> 00:13:16,440
Mob Psycho

180
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:21,220
Nii-san!

181
00:13:21,220 --> 00:13:22,910
Hey, wake up!

182
00:13:23,250 --> 00:13:24,620
Kageyama-kun!

183
00:13:24,620 --> 00:13:25,450
Mob!

184
00:13:25,450 --> 00:13:26,570
Shigeo!

185
00:13:26,570 --> 00:13:27,680
Nii-san!

186
00:13:29,030 --> 00:13:30,490
He's regained consciousness.

187
00:13:31,070 --> 00:13:32,230
Let's dig him out.

188
00:13:36,050 --> 00:13:37,790
Thank goodness you're okay.

189
00:13:37,790 --> 00:13:39,360
Unbelievable.

190
00:13:40,070 --> 00:13:43,370
Anyway, we should get away from here.

191
00:13:43,370 --> 00:13:44,210
Can you walk?

192
00:13:44,750 --> 00:13:46,010
Yes...

193
00:13:46,010 --> 00:13:49,820
All of our wounds have been healed.
Our clothes are in shambles, though.

194
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:51,430
You're right...

195
00:13:51,750 --> 00:13:54,530
Shigeo, what's up with
the left side of your chest?

196
00:13:55,660 --> 00:13:57,880
That's quite the bold fashion statement.

197
00:13:58,570 --> 00:14:02,540
Seriously... You never cease to amaze.

198
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:04,570
I do consider you my rival, you know?

199
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:07,140
Don't wander off too far.

200
00:14:13,650 --> 00:14:16,580
This ground... It's not concrete.

201
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:18,800
My mind feels all spacey.

202
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:20,960
The sky seems cramped.

203
00:14:21,430 --> 00:14:22,930
Where are we?

204
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:26,600
There's the exit. Watch out for
things that may fall onto your head.

205
00:14:27,580 --> 00:14:29,010
It's quiet.

206
00:14:29,010 --> 00:14:31,930
Surprisingly, there aren't any
news helicopters flying around.

207
00:14:31,930 --> 00:14:33,380
Well, yeah.

208
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:36,230
They're too scared to come here
when they know so little.

209
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:38,770
Everything seems fine,
even after that giant explosion.

210
00:14:38,770 --> 00:14:39,980
What's going on?

211
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:44,190
I seriously thought
you were a goner back there.

212
00:14:45,170 --> 00:14:48,570
I was sure ground zero
would've been eviscerated.

213
00:14:50,460 --> 00:14:51,790
The hell is that?

214
00:14:52,970 --> 00:14:55,370
But what appeared there happened to be...

215
00:14:55,910 --> 00:14:56,770
Hey!

216
00:14:57,240 --> 00:14:58,040
Nii-san!

217
00:14:58,220 --> 00:15:01,820
Are you okay?
Are you still actually hurt somewhere?

218
00:15:01,820 --> 00:15:05,500
Thanks, Ritsu. I think my body's okay.

219
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:08,570
But lately, whenever I use a lot of power,

220
00:15:08,570 --> 00:15:11,070
I have a hard time staying awake afterward.

221
00:15:11,070 --> 00:15:11,870
Huh?

222
00:15:15,150 --> 00:15:16,890
I'll carry you partway,

223
00:15:17,180 --> 00:15:18,280
so you can rest.

224
00:15:19,850 --> 00:15:23,190
Carry him where? Our house is...

225
00:15:23,660 --> 00:15:28,500
Sorry, he'll fix up your house,
but he'll need three days.

226
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:30,240
Just three days?!

227
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:33,930
You guys wanna come to my place?

228
00:15:33,930 --> 00:15:36,370
It'll be a bit cramped,
but I'm sure we can make it work.

229
00:15:37,460 --> 00:15:40,250
At least try to hide your displeasure, jeez.

230
00:15:40,850 --> 00:15:42,420
Oh, don't worry about me.

231
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:47,760
Could we stop by the school first?

232
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:49,970
At this hour?

233
00:15:49,970 --> 00:15:52,580
There should be a spare
tracksuit in his club room.

234
00:15:52,930 --> 00:15:55,140
Telepathy Club

235
00:15:52,930 --> 00:15:55,140
Body Improvement Club

236
00:15:57,020 --> 00:15:58,060
That must be it.

237
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:03,020
I wonder if I could borrow one for myself.

238
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:04,520
Body improvement

239
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:04,520
Lower body
strengthening month!!

240
00:16:03,020 --> 00:16:04,520
But I can't do it without asking...

241
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:07,520
Tracksuit thieves!

242
00:16:07,850 --> 00:16:08,940
Captain.

243
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:10,670
My heart just stopped!

244
00:16:12,140 --> 00:16:13,860
I see.

245
00:16:14,070 --> 00:16:18,170
I came here to get some dumbbells,
and you sure gave me a scare.

246
00:16:18,170 --> 00:16:21,120
Sorry... You scared us pretty good, too.

247
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:24,830
Put on the muscle! Burn the fat!

248
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:22,860
I understand the situation now.

249
00:16:22,860 --> 00:16:24,830
Hang on one second.

250
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:28,670
Hello? You see...

251
00:16:30,300 --> 00:16:34,390
Um... Why's everyone from
the Body Improvement Club here?

252
00:16:34,390 --> 00:16:35,890
We're about to...

253
00:16:35,890 --> 00:16:37,760
The Body Improvement Club

254
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:41,980
will now begin a three-day four-night
strengthening hell training camp!

255
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:45,230
No, we're—

256
00:16:45,230 --> 00:16:47,480
We should always help
each other out when in need!

257
00:16:47,480 --> 00:16:49,440
I mean, we're really tired—

258
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:51,820
I'm sure you want to sleep on a giant futon!

259
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:53,280
No, a small one will do just fine!

260
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:56,240
We have enough room for all
of you at my granny's house!

261
00:16:56,240 --> 00:16:59,530
You have to procure and make your own food,
so it'll be excellent training!

262
00:16:59,530 --> 00:17:01,950
And it's just a 90-minute jog away!
We'll be there in no time!

263
00:17:01,950 --> 00:17:03,040
Now, let's go!

264
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:04,580
R-Reigen-san, help...

265
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:07,540
Hey, that's great. Do your best.

266
00:17:07,750 --> 00:17:09,370
I'm gonna take a cab home.

267
00:17:10,950 --> 00:17:12,650
Body Improvement!

268
00:17:12,650 --> 00:17:15,700
Fight on! Fight on!

269
00:17:14,470 --> 00:17:15,700
How cruel...

270
00:17:17,070 --> 00:17:18,430
I totally forgot!

271
00:17:19,110 --> 00:17:21,980
I should've just gone over
to Reigen-san's place.

272
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:30,020
I wonder what that thing is.

273
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:33,700
It's even more confusing up close.

274
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:37,090
How do one of these things even grow?

275
00:17:37,090 --> 00:17:39,450
Isn't it obvious?!

276
00:17:39,440 --> 00:17:42,600
Aliens! This is the work of aliens!

277
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:45,020
Amazing.

278
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:46,460
Could this be...

279
00:17:46,710 --> 00:17:48,960
The work of our beloved leader?

280
00:17:49,970 --> 00:17:52,880
Wow... It looks like a vegetable.

281
00:17:53,750 --> 00:17:56,090
I bet Mob-kun was involved.

282
00:17:56,300 --> 00:17:57,220
I just know it.

283
00:17:58,240 --> 00:17:59,600
That's amazing!

284
00:17:59,970 --> 00:18:02,140
You're the ones behind that giant plant?

285
00:18:02,470 --> 00:18:03,870
W-Well...

286
00:18:03,870 --> 00:18:07,770
If you're asking if we were
directly involved, then no.

287
00:18:07,770 --> 00:18:09,600
We basically were, though.

288
00:18:09,600 --> 00:18:10,150
What?

289
00:18:10,150 --> 00:18:12,480
Amazing! Fantastic!

290
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:13,610
Mitsuura-san.

291
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:17,490
I think I'm going to stop coming here.

292
00:18:17,780 --> 00:18:19,950
Kurosaki-san? But why?!

293
00:18:20,150 --> 00:18:22,960
If everything goes well with your research

294
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:26,290
and you actually develop the technology
to make espers out of people,

295
00:18:26,570 --> 00:18:30,920
we might get more espers
who misuse their powers.

296
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:33,740
So I think you should just stop.

297
00:18:33,740 --> 00:18:35,390
I don't even need the money.

298
00:18:36,540 --> 00:18:38,340
I agree.

299
00:18:38,340 --> 00:18:40,950
We're actually not that impressive.

300
00:18:42,190 --> 00:18:43,310
Kids...

301
00:18:45,070 --> 00:18:46,310
All right!

302
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:49,520
I'll stop using you for research!

303
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:54,260
But to be honest, I'm just having fun

304
00:18:54,890 --> 00:18:56,690
spending time with you kids.

305
00:18:57,330 --> 00:19:01,120
You don't mind coming by once
in a while as friends, do you?

306
00:19:02,180 --> 00:19:04,830
Hey. What are you going to do now?

307
00:19:05,070 --> 00:19:07,080
The organization is gone.

308
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:09,470
I'm obviously going to have
to find another way to live.

309
00:19:09,950 --> 00:19:11,360
Yeah...

310
00:19:11,360 --> 00:19:15,810
Now that the scars on my face are gone,
maybe I'll start up a ramen shop.

311
00:19:15,810 --> 00:19:18,110
The hospitality industry is not for you.

312
00:19:18,110 --> 00:19:19,760
Just put your body to good use.

313
00:19:19,760 --> 00:19:21,850
What are you going to do, Sakurai?

314
00:19:21,850 --> 00:19:24,420
I have an interview at a convenience
store the day after tomorrow.

315
00:19:25,780 --> 00:19:27,510
What? You're going to ask him?

316
00:19:27,510 --> 00:19:31,190
Yes. I'm considering asking Master Reigen
if I can study under him for a while.

317
00:19:31,190 --> 00:19:34,440
Don't. You're really not a people person.

318
00:19:34,630 --> 00:19:37,400
I agree. You're kinda dreary.

319
00:19:40,570 --> 00:19:43,340
The government has determined that

320
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:47,920
this is the work of
a delusional criminal organization, huh?

321
00:19:48,390 --> 00:19:51,530
I can't believe you turned yourself in
after being defeated by a civilian esper.

322
00:19:52,030 --> 00:19:53,040
It's the truth.

323
00:19:54,090 --> 00:19:57,500
Man, where does that leave us pros?

324
00:19:57,990 --> 00:19:59,470
What's going to happen to my dad?

325
00:20:01,090 --> 00:20:04,250
Under normal circumstances,
he'd be executed.

326
00:20:04,650 --> 00:20:08,480
But there is a chance he'll be kept alive
as a research subject.

327
00:20:09,050 --> 00:20:12,600
Why'd he have to say that to his son?

328
00:20:12,790 --> 00:20:15,290
Well, it's not my call to make,

329
00:20:15,290 --> 00:20:17,040
so I can't say for sure.

330
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:18,610
P-P-President!

331
00:20:18,910 --> 00:20:20,140
Serizawa.

332
00:20:20,140 --> 00:20:24,320
I never actually considered
you all my comrades.

333
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:26,420
There's no reason to be worried about me.

334
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:31,020
Because you lack self-confidence,
others will find you easy to manipulate.

335
00:20:31,450 --> 00:20:32,980
Be careful from now on.

336
00:20:34,810 --> 00:20:35,460
Sho.

337
00:20:36,320 --> 00:20:40,590
I wanted you to see your mother again,

338
00:20:40,590 --> 00:20:44,000
but my pride severed that possibility.

339
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:46,460
I'm truly sorry.

340
00:20:46,860 --> 00:20:47,470
Don't be.

341
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:50,110
I see Mom every now and then.

342
00:20:51,070 --> 00:20:54,190
She's always asking me how you're doing.

343
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:59,150
I wish I could've stopped you
before she found out what you'd become.

344
00:20:59,660 --> 00:21:02,690
When I called her this morning,
she said she'd come see you sometime.

345
00:21:03,550 --> 00:21:06,570
So don't you dare think this is all over.

346
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:10,790
You still need to get an earful from Mom.

347
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:26,680
"People need other people," huh?

348
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:30,140
Spirits and Such Consultation Office

349
00:21:30,140 --> 00:21:33,100
What? It was just a short circuit?

350
00:21:33,340 --> 00:21:36,150
Apparently, a mouse bit into some wires.

351
00:21:36,150 --> 00:21:37,940
Thanks to that, the fire insurance kicked in,

352
00:21:37,940 --> 00:21:40,580
so we get a fresh start at a new office.

353
00:21:42,370 --> 00:21:45,240
But it sure looks bland right now.

354
00:21:46,290 --> 00:21:48,320
Mob, do your thing.

355
00:21:48,320 --> 00:21:49,200
Okay.

356
00:21:51,870 --> 00:21:53,190
Thanks.

357
00:21:55,910 --> 00:21:59,080
The hole in my uniform... I just remembered.

358
00:21:59,660 --> 00:22:03,110
I'd put the broccoli seeds in there.

359
00:22:04,220 --> 00:22:05,770
Broccoli?

360
00:22:05,770 --> 00:22:06,680
The seeds from back the—

361
00:22:09,850 --> 00:22:10,970
Now I see.

362
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:14,060
Master, you mean that's...

363
00:22:15,070 --> 00:22:18,510
Welp. Let's just forget we ever saw this.

364
00:22:19,670 --> 00:22:21,910
But man, he sure is late...

365
00:22:23,860 --> 00:22:25,190
Oh, there you are.

366
00:22:25,560 --> 00:22:26,840
Come in.

367
00:22:26,840 --> 00:22:29,410
I got lost. I'm very sorry.

368
00:22:29,680 --> 00:22:31,930
Thanks for the other day, Kageyama-kun.

369
00:22:32,310 --> 00:22:33,910
A suit...?

370
00:22:34,230 --> 00:22:35,870
You're going to work here?

371
00:22:36,090 --> 00:22:39,830
Yup. Reigen-san made me
an offer after all that.

372
00:22:40,060 --> 00:22:43,050
He said that there was something
that even I could do.

373
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:47,510
And it's the least I can do after
my organization caused everyone trouble.

374
00:22:50,950 --> 00:22:54,810
We're here to make a better tomorrow,
so this is perfect for you!

375
00:22:55,110 --> 00:22:57,270
Y-Yes, sir! I'll do my best!

376
00:22:57,530 --> 00:23:01,250
My client will be here soon,
but before that...

377
00:23:01,250 --> 00:23:01,980
Huh?

378
00:23:02,530 --> 00:23:04,580
We're going to have to
do something about that.

379
00:23:05,310 --> 00:23:05,990
Huh?

380
00:23:07,270 --> 00:23:09,740
Whoa, that's amazing.

381
00:23:11,130 --> 00:23:12,450
He looks so different.

382
00:23:12,680 --> 00:23:16,190
I guess he at least looks like
he can pull off customer service now.

383
00:23:16,190 --> 00:23:20,670
C-Customer service?! Wh-What should
I do when a customer shows up?!

384
00:23:20,930 --> 00:23:22,320
What did you do at your last job?

385
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:26,840
My orders were to smack them with
my umbrella if I sensed any hostility...

386
00:23:26,990 --> 00:23:28,210
The hell?

387
00:23:28,210 --> 00:23:30,540
Yeah, things aren't that different here.

388
00:23:30,540 --> 00:23:32,290
If there's anything else
you don't understand,

389
00:23:32,290 --> 00:23:33,800
go ahead and ask your senior there.

390
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:35,060
Senior?

391
00:23:35,060 --> 00:23:39,370
Mob, you show him the ropes
while he's still in training.

392
00:23:39,370 --> 00:23:39,990
Huh?

393
00:23:41,270 --> 00:23:44,230
It's a pleasure to work with you,
Kageyama-senpai!

394
00:23:44,470 --> 00:23:48,250
Huh? It's... a pleasure
to work with you, too...

395
00:23:49,120 --> 00:23:53,200
What should I do?
Now I'm getting nervous, too.

396
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:58,200
Spirits and Such Consultation Office

397
00:23:53,790 --> 00:23:55,550
Pardon me.

398
00:23:55,550 --> 00:23:58,200
Oh, hello there! Sorry about the mess.

399
00:23:58,560 --> 00:24:00,260
Please have a seat right over there.

400
00:24:00,260 --> 00:24:02,010
Serizawa, get our guest some tea.

401
00:24:02,010 --> 00:24:06,220
T-Tea? I-I'm sorry,
I've never made tea before...

402
00:24:06,220 --> 00:24:07,470
We're doomed.
